<% @title = "Amber 2 preview — Build the business, not the boilerplate" %>
<% @meta = "Preview the Amber 2 web framework, default web application path, native application preview, and character-led Crystal ecosystem." %>

<div class="release-strip preview-strip">
  <div class="site-container">
    <span class="release-pill">Preview</span>
    <span>Amber V2 experience proof — owner approval is required before release.</span>
    <a href="/docs/v2/beta-support">Review the beta boundary →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<header class="hero hero-v2" data-crystal-field>
  <div class="crystal-field" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="field-crystal field-crystal-a"></span>
    <span class="field-crystal field-crystal-b"></span>
    <span class="field-crystal field-crystal-c"></span>
    <span class="field-crystal field-crystal-d"></span>
    <span class="field-crystal field-crystal-e"></span>
    <span class="field-orbit field-orbit-a"></span>
    <span class="field-orbit field-orbit-b"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="site-container hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Amber 2 · The Crystal web framework</p>
      <h1>Build the business.<br><em>Not the boilerplate.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">Amber gives one developer a complete, typed path from idea to a running web application—with clear conventions that can grow with the business.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/v2/getting-started/installation">Start the web path</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="#application-types">Compare application types</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-proof-row" aria-label="Preview support summary">
        <span><strong>Default</strong> web application</span>
        <span><strong>Preview</strong> native application</span>
        <span><strong>Local</strong> front-end assets</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art hero-art-amber reveal" aria-label="Amber, the framework lead, building an application">
      <img src="/assets/characters/amber-hero-inviting-studio.webp" width="1536" height="1024" alt="Amber smiling beside her laptop and beckoning the visitor to join her">
      <a class="character-callout" href="/characters/amber">
        <span class="callout-kicker">Framework lead</span>
        <strong>Amber</strong>
        <span>Meet the person behind the path →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="demo-section" aria-labelledby="first-run-title">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading compact-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">First run, illustrated</p>
          <h2 id="first-run-title">From Homebrew<br>to localhost.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The web application is the default. Replay the supported two-step Homebrew install, create the app, and watch the generated page open.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="build-demo reveal" data-terminal-demo>
        <div class="terminal terminal-demo" aria-label="Amber CLI installation and first-run terminal session">
          <div class="terminal-toolbar">
            <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
            <span class="terminal-title">amber-v2 — zsh</span>
            <div class="terminal-controls">
              <button type="button" data-terminal-replay>Replay</button>
              <a href="/docs/v2/getting-started/installation">Exact guide</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-screen" aria-live="polite" data-terminal-screen>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-command" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="typed" data-terminal-text="brew tap amberframework/amber_cli"><span class="terminal-prompt">❯</span> <span class="terminal-command" data-terminal-output></span><span class="terminal-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Tapping amberframework/amber_cli"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-muted" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Tap ready — 1 formula available"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-success" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-command" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="typed" data-terminal-text="brew install amber_cli"><span class="terminal-prompt">❯</span> <span class="terminal-command" data-terminal-output></span><span class="terminal-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Downloading amber_cli 2.0.2"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-muted" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Compiling with Crystal 1.21"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-accent" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Installed /opt/homebrew/bin/amber"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-success" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-command" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="typed" data-terminal-text="amber new my_app"><span class="terminal-prompt">❯</span> <span class="terminal-command" data-terminal-output></span><span class="terminal-comment"> # web is the default</span><span class="terminal-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Created my_app · Amber 2.0.0-beta.2"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-accent" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-command" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="typed" data-terminal-text="cd my_app && amber watch"><span class="terminal-prompt">❯</span> <span class="terminal-command" data-terminal-output></span><span class="terminal-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-output" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="system" data-terminal-text="Resolving dependencies · compiling my_app"><span class="terminal-state" data-terminal-state>⠋</span> <span class="terminal-muted" data-terminal-output></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-line terminal-line-ready" data-terminal-line data-terminal-mode="ready" data-terminal-text="Listening at"><span class="terminal-state terminal-state-ready" data-terminal-state>◆</span> <span class="terminal-success" data-terminal-output></span> <button class="terminal-url" type="button" data-terminal-url aria-label="Open the generated application preview">http://localhost:3000</button></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="app-preview-window" data-app-preview aria-label="Generated Amber application preview">
          <div class="browser-toolbar">
            <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
            <div class="browser-address">http://localhost:3000</div>
          </div>
          <div class="generated-app-page">
            <div class="welcome">
            <h1>Welcome to my_app!</h1>
            <p>Your Amber V2 beta web application is running.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Edit <code>src/views/home/index.ecr</code></li>
              <li>Add routes in <code>config/routes.cr</code></li>
              <li>Run <code>crystal spec</code> before committing</li>
            </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tinted" id="application-types">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Choose the application</p>
          <h2>Web by default.<br>Native when invited.</h2>
        </div>
        <p><code>amber new my_app</code> makes the supported web application. Amber CLI also exposes a separate native preview; the interface labels the difference instead of burying it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="app-type-grid">
        <article class="app-type-card app-type-default reveal" data-tilt>
          <div class="app-type-heading"><span class="app-type-icon">&lt;/&gt;</span><span class="status-badge">Default · V2 beta</span></div>
          <h3>Web application</h3>
          <p>HTTP server, routes, controllers, ECR views, locally served CSS and JavaScript, configuration, and the complete first-run path.</p>
          <pre><code>amber new my_app
# equivalent to --type web</code></pre>
          <a href="/docs/v2/guides/web-template">Inspect the generated web template →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="app-type-card app-type-preview reveal" data-tilt>
          <div class="app-type-heading"><span class="app-type-icon">◇</span><span class="status-badge">Explicit preview</span></div>
          <h3>Native application</h3>
          <p>A cross-platform preview for macOS, iOS, and Android using Asset Pipeline UI, FSDD process managers, crystal-audio, and platform build scripts.</p>
          <pre><code>amber new field_app --type native</code></pre>
          <span class="boundary-copy">Not release-gated with the web beta. Evaluate it as a separate preview.</span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Framework core</p>
          <h2>Opinionated where<br>the path should be clear.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Amber keeps the essential pieces close enough to understand: compiled routes, typed configuration, ECR views, request schemas, and a first-party application structure.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card reveal" data-tilt><span class="feature-icon">A</span><h3>Typed configuration</h3><p>Catch configuration mistakes at startup and keep environment behavior explicit.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal" data-tilt><span class="feature-icon">{ }</span><h3>Compiled routing</h3><p>Describe HTTP routes with a focused DSL backed by Crystal’s compiler.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal" data-tilt><span class="feature-icon">&lt;%</span><h3>ECR-first views</h3><p>Render server-side HTML with Crystal’s native embedded templates.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal" data-tilt><span class="feature-icon">↗</span><h3>Schema API</h3><p>Keep request and response contracts close to the application code that uses them.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal" data-tilt><span class="feature-icon">⚡</span><h3>Crystal performance</h3><p>Compile to a native binary and use Crystal 1.21’s multithreaded runtime.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal" data-tilt><span class="feature-icon">CLI</span><h3>One development loop</h3><p>Install, generate, test, build, and watch from a purpose-built Amber CLI.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section grant-spotlight-section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="grant-spotlight reveal">
        <div class="grant-spotlight-art">
          <img src="/assets/characters/grant-id-original-studio.webp" width="800" height="800" alt="Grant, Amber's records specialist, organizing the application data layer">
          <span class="grant-file-stamp">AF-014 · Records</span>
        </div>
        <div class="grant-spotlight-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Ecosystem preview · persistence</p>
          <h2>Grant keeps the records straight.</h2>
          <p>When an application needs a relational data layer, Grant is the V2 ecosystem path for models, migrations, relations, validations, callbacks, and queries. The core web template does not install an ORM by default, so the preview stays an intentional choice.</p>
          <div class="grant-capabilities" aria-label="Grant preview capabilities">
            <span>Typed models</span><span>Auditable migrations</span><span>Readable queries</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grant-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/v2/guides/models/grant">Evaluate the Grant preview</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/characters/grant">Meet Grant</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section crew-section">
    <div class="site-container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Amber and friends</p>
          <h2>Software boundaries,<br>with personality.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The personnel files make each responsibility memorable while keeping the actual release boundaries and documentation one click away.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="crew-roster crew-roster-home">
        <a class="personnel-card personnel-amber reveal" href="/characters/amber" data-tilt>
          <div class="personnel-photo"><img src="/assets/characters/amber-id-original-studio.webp" width="800" height="800" alt="Portrait of Amber"></div>
          <div class="personnel-file"><span class="file-label">AF-001 · Framework lead</span><h3>Amber</h3><p>Turns the business idea into the application people can see and use.</p><span class="status-badge">V2 beta core</span><span class="file-link">Open file · Read docs →</span></div>
        </a>
        <a class="personnel-card personnel-grant reveal" href="/characters/grant" data-tilt>
          <div class="personnel-photo"><img src="/assets/characters/grant-id-original-studio.webp" width="800" height="800" alt="Portrait of Grant"></div>
          <div class="personnel-file"><span class="file-label">AF-014 · Records</span><h3>Grant</h3><p>Keeps models, relations, migrations, and queries organized.</p><span class="status-badge">Ecosystem preview</span><span class="file-link">Open file · Read docs →</span></div>
        </a>
        <a class="personnel-card personnel-gemma reveal" href="/characters/gemma" data-tilt>
          <div class="personnel-photo"><img src="/assets/characters/gemma-id-original-studio.webp" width="800" height="800" alt="Portrait of Gemma"></div>
          <div class="personnel-file"><span class="file-label">AF-027 · Files</span><h3>Gemma</h3><p>Moves attachments from validation through storage and delivery.</p><span class="status-badge">Ecosystem preview</span><span class="file-link">Open file · Read docs →</span></div>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="crew-actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/characters">Meet the whole crew</a><span>Background-job casting remains proposed.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container amber-way-panel reveal">
      <img src="/assets/characters/amber-chibi-original-studio.webp" width="800" height="800" alt="Chibi Amber holding a laptop and pointing">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The philosophy behind the defaults</p>
        <h2>Learn Amber's Way.</h2>
        <p>Productivity. Performance. Happiness. Humility. Respect. Trust. The product values and community commitments that shape Amber.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/amber-way">Read the six principles</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
